  "auditory_note": "Tap ▶ Listen to play each clip.",
  "teach": {
    "intro": {
      "en": "Hi Evan! Today is a practice day with no new words. Many greetings, family words, and small words need more practice, so we bring them back and use them in short sentences you can say to your family. The review words are woven right into the lesson.",
      "py": "Nǐ hǎo, Evan! Jīntiān shì liànxí rì, méiyǒu xīn cí. Hěn duō wènhòu cí, jiārén cí hé xiǎo cí xūyào duō liànxí, suǒyǐ wǒmen bǎ tāmen dài huílái, yòng zài nǐ kěyǐ duì jiārén shuō de duǎn jùzi lǐ. Fùxí de cí jiù zài kèwén lǐmiàn."
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Greeting my family: words to bring back"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "Today there are no new words. We bring back greetings, family, and a few small words that have slipped, like hello, thank you, goodbye, one, four, and apple. Listen to each one, then say it out loud.",
        "py": "Jīntiān méiyǒu xīn cí. Wǒmen bǎ wènhòu cí, jiārén cí hé yìxiē wàngdiào de xiǎo cí dài huílái, bǐrú nǐ hǎo, xièxie, zàijiàn, yī, sì hé píngguǒ. Měi gè cí xiān tīng, ránhòu dàshēng shuō."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Greetings"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "hello",
        "py": "nǐ hǎo",
        "note_en": "Nǐ hǎo: two 3rd tones in a row. Say the first one like 2nd tone: ní hǎo.",
        "note_py": "Nǐ hǎo: liǎng gè dì-sān shēng. Dì-yī gè niàn chéng dì-èr shēng: ní hǎo.",
        "listen_url": "l21-nihao.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "thank you",
        "py": "xièxie",
        "note_en": "Xièxie: 4th tone, then a light second syllable.",
        "note_py": "Xièxie: dì-sì shēng, dì-èr gè zì qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-xiexie.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "goodbye",
        "py": "zàijiàn",
        "note_en": "Zàijiàn: both syllables are 4th tone, short and falling.",
        "note_py": "Zàijiàn: liǎng gè dōu shì dì-sì shēng, duǎn ér xià jiàng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-zaijian.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "very",
        "py": "hěn",
        "note_en": "Hěn goes before the describing word: Wǒ hěn hǎo = I am (very) good.",
        "note_py": "Hěn fàng zài xíngróngcí qiánmiàn: Wǒ hěn hǎo.",
        "listen_url": "l21-hen.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "good",
        "py": "hǎo",
        "note_en": "Hǎo is 3rd tone, low and dipping.",
        "note_py": "Hǎo shì dì-sān shēng, dī ér wān.",
        "listen_url": "l21-hao.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Family and people"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "dad",
        "py": "bàba",
        "note_en": "Bàba: 4th tone, then a light second syllable.",
        "note_py": "Bàba: dì-sì shēng, hòu miàn qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-baba.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "mom",
        "py": "māma",
        "note_en": "Māma: 1st tone, then a light second syllable. Not mā by itself, which is the tone demo.",
        "note_py": "Māma: dì-yī shēng, hòu miàn qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-mama.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "younger sister",
        "py": "mèimei",
        "note_en": "Mèimei: 4th tone, then light. Mèi = younger sister.",
        "note_py": "Mèimei: dì-sì shēng, hòu miàn qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-meimei.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "older sister",
        "py": "jiějie",
        "note_en": "Jiějie: 3rd tone, then light. Say the first one a bit higher: jiéjie.",
        "note_py": "Jiějie: dì-sān shēng, hòu miàn qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-jiejie.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "grandma (father's mother)",
        "py": "nǎinai",
        "note_en": "Nǎinai: 3rd tone, then light.",
        "note_py": "Nǎinai: dì-sān shēng, hòu miàn qīng shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-nainai.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Small words, food, and animals"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "one",
        "py": "yī",
        "note_en": "Yī alone is 1st tone. Before a 4th tone word like gè it changes to yí: yí gè.",
        "note_py": "Yī dānduó shì dì-yī shēng. Zài gè qiánmiàn biàn chéng yí: yí gè.",
        "listen_url": "l21-yi.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "four",
        "py": "sì",
        "note_en": "Sì is 4th tone, sharp and falling. Do not mix it up with shí (ten).",
        "note_py": "Sì shì dì-sì shēng, duǎn ér xià jiàng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-si.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "apple",
        "py": "píngguǒ",
        "note_en": "Píngguǒ: 2nd tone, then 3rd tone.",
        "note_py": "Píngguǒ: dì-èr shēng jiā dì-sān shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-pingguo.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "vegetable / dish",
        "py": "cài",
        "note_en": "Cài is 4th tone. Wǒ chī cài = I eat vegetables.",
        "note_py": "Cài shì dì-sì shēng. Wǒ chī cài.",
        "listen_url": "l21-cai.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "white",
        "py": "báisè",
        "note_en": "Báisè: 2nd tone, then 4th tone.",
        "note_py": "Báisè: dì-èr shēng, ránhòu dì-sì shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l21-baise.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "animal",
        "py": "dòngwù",
        "note_en": "Dòngwù: 4th tone twice. Māo shì dòngwù = A cat is an animal.",
        "note_py": "Dòngwù: liǎng gè dì-sì shēng. Māo shì dòngwù.",
        "listen_url": "l21-dongwu.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Sentences to say"
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "Hello, dad! Hello, mom!",
        "py": "Nǐ hǎo, bàba! Nǐ hǎo, māma!",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex1.mp3",
        "n": 1
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "How are you? I am very good, thank you!",
        "py": "Nǐ hǎo ma? Wǒ hěn hǎo, xièxie!",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex2.mp3",
        "n": 2
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "My younger sister eats an apple.",
        "py": "Wǒ de mèimei chī yí gè píngguǒ.",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex3.mp3",
        "n": 3
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "Grandma eats vegetables.",
        "py": "Nǎinai chī cài.",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex4.mp3",
        "n": 4
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "I have an older sister and four apples.",
        "py": "Wǒ yǒu yí gè jiějie, sì gè píngguǒ.",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex5.mp3",
        "n": 5
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "A cat is an animal.",
        "py": "Māo shì dòngwù.",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex6.mp3",
        "n": 6
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "Goodbye, grandma!",
        "py": "Zàijiàn, nǎinai!",
        "listen_url": "l21-ex7.mp3",
        "n": 7
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "kind": "pattern",
        "title": "Pattern: greet + person, say how you are",
        "body_en": "To greet someone, say nǐ hǎo and then the person: Nǐ hǎo, bàba! To say how you are, use wǒ hěn hǎo. To count, use a number plus gè: yí gè, sì gè.",
        "body_py": "Wènhòu biéren, shuō nǐ hǎo, ránhòu shuō rén: Nǐ hǎo, bàba! Shuō zìjǐ zěnmeyàng, yòng wǒ hěn hǎo. Shùshù yòng shùzì jiā gè: yí gè, sì gè."
      }
    ]
  },
